WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.872 --> 00:00:05.075
Line 3 has to stand in hall B before the summer shutdown ends.

2
00:00:05.789 --> 00:00:08.401
The power comes from an installer from outside.

3
00:00:09.405 --> 00:00:12.110
But he says he can only come after the shutdown.

4
00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:14.848
Without power the line cannot run.

5
00:00:15.812 --> 00:00:17.008
How do you make the date?

6
00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.892
We follow this project through the four topics of the module.

7
00:00:22.211 --> 00:00:25.938
The first topic is preparing, with interests and alternatives.

8
00:00:26.664 --> 00:00:29.903
The installer says it can only happen after the shutdown.

9
00:00:30.987 --> 00:00:32.276
That is his position.

10
00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:36.528
His interest is that his crew works for another client first.

11
00:00:37.572 --> 00:00:40.231
Find an option that serves his interest too.

12
00:00:40.911 --> 00:00:43.605
The plant digs the trench for the cable itself.

13
00:00:44.308 --> 00:00:46.816
That costs you little and saves him a lot.

14
00:00:47.912 --> 00:00:49.259
And if he keeps saying no?

15
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.594
Then your alternative is a second installer.

16
00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.567
For preparing we use a BATNA and a fair standard.

17
00:00:57.893 --> 00:01:01.272
The second topic is at the table, offers and trades.

18
00:01:01.974 --> 00:01:03.518
The installer will come sooner,

19
00:01:03.669 --> 00:01:07.373
but wants a surcharge because his crew then works at the weekend.

20
00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.591
The buyer pays for that from a cut budget.

21
00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:15.886
He names a figure first, and that number pulls the outcome towards it.

22
00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:19.754
Do not argue about his number, ask what it rests on.

23
00:01:20.535 --> 00:01:23.461
Then put your own figure on the table, with a reason.

24
00:01:24.491 --> 00:01:27.521
After that you give ground, in ever smaller steps.

25
00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:31.840
At the table we use an anchor and a conditional concession.

26
00:01:33.209 --> 00:01:36.170
The third topic is scope, fees and clients.

27
00:01:36.861 --> 00:01:40.727
The sponsor asks whether the lighting of line 4 can be added too,

28
00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.176
because everything only stands still during the shutdown.

29
00:01:45.247 --> 00:01:47.302
Scope, time and cost hang together.

30
00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.291
If one moves, something else has to.

31
00:01:51.141 --> 00:01:55.635
You do not refuse, you make the trade visible and let the sponsor choose.

32
00:01:56.673 --> 00:01:59.970
The buyer has to save and asks for a discount on your fee.

33
00:02:00.635 --> 00:02:02.876
Keep your fee and do less for less money.

34
00:02:03.894 --> 00:02:07.806
With clients we use the iron triangle and a change request.

35
00:02:09.145 --> 00:02:11.270
The fourth topic is holding your ground.

36
00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.607
The first order is waiting,

37
00:02:13.735 --> 00:02:16.242
so to make the date the sponsor wants to skip

38
00:02:16.324 --> 00:02:18.704
the safety inspection of the power cabinet.

39
00:02:19.755 --> 00:02:22.344
First say yes to what you protect, safety.

40
00:02:23.117 --> 00:02:24.499
Then say a clear no.

41
00:02:25.205 --> 00:02:29.849
After that say yes to something else, the inspection right after the connection.

42
00:02:30.846 --> 00:02:33.691
You do not trade safety, not even for the date.

43
00:02:34.479 --> 00:02:35.617
That is a red line.

44
00:02:36.591 --> 00:02:39.436
We use a positive no and the conflict modes.

45
00:02:40.782 --> 00:02:41.664
It connects.

46
00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:44.407
You prepare and bid at the table.

47
00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:49.030
You keep scope and fee in balance and hold your ground where you must.

48
00:02:50.059 --> 00:02:52.613
The installer now comes during the shutdown,

49
00:02:52.753 --> 00:02:54.785
for a surcharge the buyer can live with.

50
00:02:55.525 --> 00:03:00.019
The inspection stays, the lighting of line 4 follows after the shutdown,

51
00:03:00.181 --> 00:03:02.375
and line 3 gets into place.

52
00:03:03.711 --> 00:03:05.348
This is the map of Projects.

53
00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:11.141
Negotiating and holding your ground is the third station of People and influence.

54
00:03:12.179 --> 00:03:15.325
This module has four topics, each with four levels.

55
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:18.817
Start with preparing, at Basics level.

56
00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.984
At Working knowledge you add ZOPA, splitting the difference,

57
00:03:23.134 --> 00:03:26.292
payment terms and appreciation without deference.

58
00:03:27.384 --> 00:03:31.309
At Advanced you add the preparation sheet, trading across issues,

59
00:03:31.506 --> 00:03:33.758
assumptions and the fact-view-request.

60
00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:36.841
At Expert you add a weaker position,

61
00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:40.453
hard tactics, renegotiating and the golden bridge.

62
00:03:41.466 --> 00:03:45.599
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
